# Defect 508 and panel 199's R2, ratified 2026-10-09: a function that calls
# itself through a function value ran at `-O2` until `timeout` stopped it
# (exit 124), the call in tail position turned into a jump, where `-O0`
# printed `panic: stack exhausted` (134). The `-O2` words keep a call a call
# (`-fno-optimize-sibling-calls`), and it aborts at every level. `check` lets
# it through: a call through a function value is not the function, to
# `endless_recursion` (panel 199's R7, filed apart). Under the sanitiser the
# runtime's guard yields to ASan, which says `stack-overflow`.
# Corrected 2026-10-09, defect 520 and panel 201's R3, ratified: `check`
# refuses it now, `endless_recursion`, and the case moved from `run/` to
# `check/`; what aborts at every level since is a cycle with a way out it
# never takes, `run/fixedbugs-520-...`, the witness that replaced this one.
function go(n: i64) -> i64
    f = go
    return f(n)  #~ endless_recursion

function main()
    print(go(1))
